{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"Prerequisites: Proficiency with a finesse martial weapon, 15 Dexterity\n\nYou can move around your enemies, almost like if you were dancing. As a bonus action on your turn, while wielding a finesse martial weapon in one hand and nothing in the other and not wearing heavy armor or having a reduction in speed, you may enter the \"Duelist\u0027s Dance\" to use the benefits of this feat for one minute. When you do so, you gain the following benefits:\n\n- Once per turn when you make an attack, you may choose to move 15 feet of movement that does not count against your remaining movement. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks.\n\n- If you have space to move, you can try to dodge certain incoming melee attacks (before the attack roll is made). Once per turn when you are targeted by a melee attack, you can make a Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against a DC equal to 8 + the Proficiency Bonus of the attacker if it is proficient in the attack + the Ability Modifier used for the attack. On a success, you can move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks, successfully dodging the attack, and the creature automatically misses this attack.","level":1}],"id":"Customdb2a70ca-c760-4c17-b1a8-50be51e2eceb","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Duelist\u0027s Dance [SM]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}